        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Yonin-Kan',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Yonin-Kan ('4-player Kan') is a Japanese trick-taking game from Aomori prefecture. 4 players. 40-card deck (remove 2-4s and 5â™ ). 10 each. Secret partnerships: Joker holder + J of trumps holder = 'kankei' team (revealed when played). Rotating trump sequence: â™£â†’â™¦â†’â™¥. Also called Damari-Kan ('Silent Kan').",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Kan is a popular card game in Aomori prefecture in Japan, especially at Goshogawara and Tsugaru. Yonin-Kan is the four-player variant, also called Damari-Kan (silent kan) because the Joker holder and Jack-of-trumps holder form a secret partnership and do not announce themselves until those cards are played.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40 cards: remove 2-4 of all suits + 5â™ . Include Joker.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dealer shuffles and deals ten cards to each player, one at a time (40-card pack, four players).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
